              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:Source: authException.getMessage(), which can contain user-controlled data (e.g., username) depending on the AuthenticationProvider. Sink: response.sendError(401, msg) at line 31. Dataflow: The exception message flows directly into the sendError method. Many servlet containers reflect this message in a default HTML error page without escaping. Given this is WebGoat and lacks security headers, this is a valid reflected XSS vulnerability in the context of container-generated error pages. Conclusion: Confirmed."
            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-xss",
          "ruleIndex": 7,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Source: authException.getMessage(), which can contain user-controlled data (e.g., username) depending on the AuthenticationProvider. Sink: response.sendError(401, msg) at line 31. Dataflow: The exception message flows directly into the sendError method. Many servlet containers reflect this message in a default HTML error page without escaping. Given this is WebGoat and lacks security headers, this is a valid reflected XSS vulnerability in the context of container-generated error pages. Conclusion: Confirmed."
          },
